    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1956-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By Vieta’s formulas, the product of the two roots is \\(\\frac{c}{a}.\\) Reciprocal roots have product \\(1,\\) so \\[ \\frac ca=1, \\] which requires \\(c=a.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "If the roots are \\(r\\) and \\(s,\\) reciprocal roots satisfy \\(rs=1\\)",
        "Use Vieta’s formula \\(rs=\\frac{c}{a}\\)"
      ],
